              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Spanish for the age of majority, then the Spanish for to grow old."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la vejez",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la vejez — \"old age\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Vivió una vejez tranquila en el campo. He lived a quiet old age in the country."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vejez is built on viejo 'old' with the ending -ez. Viejo is inherited from Latin vetulus, from vetus 'old' (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
